@* AdminUsers.razor — Phase 6.1

   Staff-facing user-management page at route `/Admin/Users`. Reached from
   the sidebar's "Admin → Manage Users" link (already wired in
   MainLayout.razor, role-gated to Admin/Manager/Employee). The page is also
   independently gated by [Authorize(Roles=...)] as defense-in-depth.

   PURPOSE:
     This page is the admin/manager/employee's view of every user in the
     system (staff and customers). It exists so they can:
       1. See ALL users in a compact, paginated table.
       2. Filter by Worker ID, Full Name (text filter), Gender, Group,
          and Status (dropdown filters with colored tags).
       3. Activate or Deactivate a user (soft-delete / restore).
       4. Reset a user's password (Admin only).
       5. View a user's detail page (where group changes, role edits,
          and other per-user actions live — see UserDetail.razor).

   GROUP CHANGES:
     The inline "Change group" editor that previously lived in this table
     was removed — group changes now happen on the UserDetail page
     (/Admin/Users/{Id}) where the full role-scope rules can be applied
     with the CreateUser-style Existing/New group button UI. This page
     is read-only with respect to groups: it shows the current group
     badge and lets the viewer navigate to the detail page to change it.

   FILTERING (ERP pattern):
     All filtering is client-side via Radzen's built-in filter row
     (AllowFiltering=true, FilterMode=SimpleWithMenu). Each column has
     its own filter input in a dedicated filter row beneath the header:
       - Worker ID  → text filter (Radzen default)
       - Full Name  → text filter (Radzen default)
       - Gender     → dropdown with colored tags (Male=blue, Female=pink)
       - Group      → dropdown of available groups (no colored tags)
       - Status     → dropdown with colored tags (Active=green, Inactive=red)
     The grid loads ALL users once (PageSize=500 in the backend query)
     and Radzen handles filtering + paging client-side. Same approach
     as the ERP project's SalesList page.

   ACTIVATE / DEACTIVATE FLOW:
     - A single toggle button per row. When the user is Active, the button
       shows "Deactivate" (Danger, block icon). When Inactive, it shows
       "Activate" (Success, check_circle icon).
     - Self-deactivation is blocked client-side (button hidden on the
       current user's own row) AND server-side (handler rejects it).
     - MANAGER SCOPE (Phase 6.3, updated 6.4): A Manager (non-Admin) can
       activate/deactivate users in the Employee OR Customer role. The
       activate/deactivate button is HIDDEN on rows for other managers,
       admins, and read-onlys. A small "lock" icon with a tooltip replaces
       the button on those rows so the manager understands why it's missing.
       Admins see the button on every row except their own.

   RESET PASSWORD FLOW:
     - Admin-only (button hidden from Managers). Also hidden on the
       current user's own row (confusing UX).
     - On click: opens an inline modal dialog (same UX as UserDetail.razor's
       Reset Password modal — overlay + dialog + password input with
       show/hide toggle + inline validation + Cancel/Submit footer). The
       previous implementation used the browser's native JS prompt(), which
       was ugly, unstyled, un-themeable, and didn't render localized text
       correctly in some browsers.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings go through IStringLocalizer<AdminUsers>
     (Loc). Keys in AdminUsers.en-US.resx + AdminUsers.fa-IR.resx.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All actions use Wolverine command dispatch
     over the Blazor circuit. *@

@page "/Admin/Users"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@attribute [SuppressMessage("Usage", "BL0005:Component parameters should not be set outside their component", Justification = "Radzen exposes FilterValue/FilterOperator on RadzenDataGridColumn as the official programmatic filter API per https://radzen.com/documentation/blazor/data-grid-programmatic-filter/. The BL0005 analyzer (designed for plain Blazor component params) does not understand this Radzen-specific contract; the mutations are intentional and load-bearing.")]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Users.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ActivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.DeactivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ResetUserPassword
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetUsersPaginated
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@using TakOne.WebUI.Components.Dialogs.DeactivateUserDialog
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<AdminUsers> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject ErrorDisplayService ErrorDisplay
@inject Radzen.DialogService DialogService

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .admin-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .worker-id-cell {
                font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
            }

            .user-name-cell {
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .group-cell-none {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            .row-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.25rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                align-items: center;
            }

            /* Restricted-action indicator — shown in place of the activate/
                                                   deactivate button when the current user is a Manager and the
                                                   row's user is NOT in the Employee or Customer role. Mirrors the
                                                   size of the text buttons it replaces so the Actions column
                                                   doesn't jump around when scrolling between rows. */
            .row-action-locked {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                width: 32px;
                height: 32px;
                color: var(--rz-text-tertiary-color, #9ca3af);
                cursor: help;
            }

            /* ── Reset Password modal (mirrors UserDetail.razor's modal) ──
                           Inline modal dialog for resetting a user's password from the
                           admin users list. Same visual structure as UserDetail's modal
                           (overlay + dialog + header/body/footer) so admins get the same
                           UX whether they're on the list page or the detail page. The
                           previous implementation used JS prompt() which was ugly,
                           unstyled, un-themeable, and not localizable properly.

                           CSS copied verbatim from UserDetail.razor so the two pages
                           render identical modals. If you change one, change the other. */
            .modal-overlay {
                position: fixed;
                inset: 0;
                background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                z-index: 1050;
                padding: 1rem;
                animation: modal-fade-in 0.15s ease-out;
            }

            @@keyframes modal-fade-in {
                from {
                    opacity: 0;
                }

                to {
                    opacity: 1;
                }
            }

            .modal-dialog {
                background: var(--rz-background-color, #fff);
                border-radius: 8px;
                box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
                width: 100%;
                max-width: 480px;
                max-height: calc(100vh - 2rem);
                overflow-y: auto;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                animation: modal-slide-up 0.2s ease-out;
            }

            @@keyframes modal-slide-up {
                from {
                    transform: translateY(20px);
                    opacity: 0;
                }

                to {
                    transform: translateY(0);
                    opacity: 1;
                }
            }

            .modal-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
            }

            .modal-title {
                margin: 0;
                font-size: 1.125rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-text-color, #212121);
            }

            .modal-close-btn {
                background: transparent;
                border: none;
                cursor: pointer;
                padding: 0.25rem;
                line-height: 1;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 1.25rem;
                border-radius: 4px;
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
            }

                .modal-close-btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
                    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
                    color: var(--rz-text-color);
                }

                .modal-close-btn:disabled {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                    cursor: not-allowed;
                }

            .modal-body {
                padding: 1.25rem;
                flex: 1 1 auto;
            }

            .modal-body-text {
                margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.9375rem;
                line-height: 1.5;
            }

            .modal-label {
                display: block;
                margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .modal-validation {
                min-height: 1.25rem;
                margin-top: 0.5rem;
                font-size: 0.8125rem;
            }

            .modal-validation-error {
                color: var(--rz-danger, #f44336);
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

            .modal-footer {
                display: flex;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
                border-top: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
            }

            @@media (max-width: 576px) {
                .modal-footer {
                    flex-direction: column-reverse;
                }

                    .modal-footer .rz-button {
                        width: 100%;
                    }
            }

            .modal-password-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: stretch;
            }

                .modal-password-row .modal-password-field {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                    min-width: 0;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <div class="admin-header">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="group" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CreateUserButton"]"
                      Icon="person_add"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                      Visible="@(_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly)"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
    </div>

    @* ── Loading spinner ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingText"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error banner ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadUsersAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── User table ──
       Radzen built-in filter row (AllowFiltering + FilterMode.SimpleWithMenu).
       Worker ID and Full Name use Radzen's default text filter. Gender,
       Group, and Status use custom FilterTemplate dropdowns with colored
       badge tags. Paging is built-in (AllowPaging, PageSize=20). Data is
       loaded all at once (PageSize=500 in the backend query) and filtered
       client-side — same approach as the ERP SalesList page. *@
    else
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="admin-users-grid" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <RadzenDataGrid @ref="grid"
                            Data="@_users"
                            TItem="UserListItemDto"
                            AllowSorting="true"
                            AllowFiltering="true"
                            FilterMode="FilterMode.SimpleWithMenu"
                            FilterCaseSensitivity="FilterCaseSensitivity.CaseInsensitive"
                            AllowPaging="true"
                            PageSize="20"
                            PagerHorizontalAlign="HorizontalAlign.Center"
                            EmptyText="@Loc["EmptyText"]"
                            Style="width: 100%;"
                            RowRender="@OnRowRender">
                <Columns>

                    @* ── Worker ID — text filter (Radzen default) ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="WorkerId"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColWorkerId"]"
                                          Width="160px">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <span class="worker-id-cell">@(CultureFormat.FormatDigits(user.WorkerId))</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Full Name — text filter (Radzen default) ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="FullName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColFullName"]"
                                          Width="*">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <span class="user-name-cell">@user.FullName</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Gender — dropdown filter with colored tags ──
                       Male=blue badge, Female=pink badge. The dropdown's
                       ValueTemplate shows the selected value as a colored
                       badge; Template shows each option as a colored badge.
                       AllowClear resets to null (All genders). The filter
                       is client-side via column.FilterValue. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="Gender"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColGender"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetGenderLabel(user.Gender)"
                                         BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                         Style="@GetGenderBadgeStyle(user.Gender)"
                                         IsPill="true" />
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="@_selectedGenderFilter"
                                            Data="@_genderFilterOptions"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            TextProperty="Label"
                                            ValueProperty="Key"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["GenderAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnGenderFilterChanged(_selectedGenderFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 110px;">
                                <ValueTemplate Context="selected">
                                    @{
                                        var selectedStr = selected?.ToString();
                                    }
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedStr))
                                    {
                                        <RadzenBadge Text="@GetGenderLabel(selectedStr)"
                                                     BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                                     Style="@GetGenderBadgeStyle(selectedStr)"
                                                     IsPill="true" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@Loc["GenderAll"]</span>
                                    }
                                </ValueTemplate>
                                <Template Context="option">
                                    @{
                                        var item = (GenderFilterOption)option;
                                    }
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@item.Label"
                                                 BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                                 Style="@GetGenderBadgeStyle(item.Key)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDropDown>
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Group — dropdown filter, no colored tags ──
                       Plain dropdown listing all available groups (derived
                       from the loaded users). AllowClear resets to null
                       (All groups). Filter is client-side via
                       column.FilterValue. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="GroupName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColGroup"]"
                                          Width="180px"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(user.GroupName))
                            {
                                <span class="group-cell-none">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@user.GroupName"
                                             BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base"
                                             IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="@_selectedGroupFilter"
                                            Data="@_availableGroups"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["GroupAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnGroupFilterChanged(_selectedGroupFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 130px;" />
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Status — dropdown filter with colored tags ──
                       Active=green badge, Inactive=red badge. The dropdown
                       uses string keys ("Active"/"Inactive") which are
                       mapped to booleans for the IsActive column filter.
                       AllowClear resets to null (All statuses). *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="IsActive"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColStatus"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(user.IsActive)"
                                         BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(user.IsActive)"
                                         IsPill="true" />
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="@_selectedStatusFilter"
                                            Data="@_statusFilterOptions"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["StatusAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnStatusFilterChanged(_selectedStatusFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 130px;">
                                <ValueTemplate Context="selected">
                                    @{
                                        var selectedStr = selected?.ToString();
                                    }
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedStr))
                                    {
                                        <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(selectedStr)"
                                                     BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(selectedStr)"
                                                     IsPill="true" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@Loc["StatusAll"]</span>
                                    }
                                </ValueTemplate>
                                <Template Context="statusOption">
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(statusOption)"
                                                 BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(statusOption)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDropDown>
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Actions ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColActions"]"
                                          Width="220px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          Sortable="false"
                                          Filterable="false">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <div class="row-actions">
                                @* View details — navigates to user detail page.
                                   All viewers (Admin/Manager/Employee) can navigate;
                                   the detail page enforces its own per-action gates. *@
                                <RadzenButton Icon="visibility"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                              title="@Loc["ActionViewDetail"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["ActionViewDetail"]"
                                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo($"/Admin/Users/{user.Id}", forceLoad: false))" />

                                @* Activate / Deactivate toggle.
                                   Hidden on the current user's own row —
                                   self-deactivation is rejected by the
                                   handler anyway, but the button adds
                                   confusing UX so we just don't show it.
                                   When the user is Active → show Deactivate
                                   (Danger, block icon). When Inactive → show
                                   Activate (Success, check_circle icon).

                                   MANAGER SCOPE (Phase 6.3, updated 6.4):
                                   If the current user is a Manager (not
                                   Admin), the button is only shown on rows
                                   whose user is in the Employee OR Customer
                                   role. On other rows (managers, admins,
                                   read-onlys), a small "lock" icon with a
                                   tooltip replaces the button so the manager
                                   understands why it's missing. Admins see
                                   the button on every row except their own.

                                   EMPLOYEE VIEWERS (Phase 6.5):
                                   Employees can't activate/deactivate anyone —
                                   the button is hidden on every row AND no
                                   lock icon is shown (the lock is a Manager-only
                                   affordance; for Employees the entire
                                   activate/deactivate feature is off-limits,
                                   so showing locks everywhere would be noisy). *@
                                @if (user.Id != _currentUserId && (_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly))
                                {
                                    @if (CanActOn(user))
                                    {
                                        @if (user.IsActive)
                                        {
                                            <RadzenButton Icon="block"
                                                          Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                          title="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                          aria-label="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                          Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                          Click="@(() => HandleDeactivateAsync(user))" />
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <RadzenButton Icon="check_circle"
                                                          Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                                          title="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                                          aria-label="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                                          Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                          Click="@(() => HandleActivateAsync(user))" />
                                        }
                                    }
                                    else if (_isManagerOnly)
                                    {
                                        @* Manager can't act on this row — show a lock icon
                                           with a tooltip explaining why. aria-label gives
                                           screen readers the same explanation. Only shown
                                           for Managers (not Employees) since Employees
                                           can't activate/deactivate anyone — locks would
                                           be noisy. *@
                                        <span class="row-action-locked"
                                              title="@Loc["ActionLockedForManager"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["ActionLockedForManager"]">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="lock" Style="font-size: 1.1rem;" />
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                }

                                @* Reset password — Admin only. *@
                                @if (_isAdmin && user.Id != _currentUserId)
                                {
                                    <RadzenButton Icon="vpn_key"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                                  title="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                                  aria-label="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                                  Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleResetPasswordAsync(user))" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                </Columns>
            </RadzenDataGrid>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Reset Password modal ──
       Inline modal dialog for resetting a user's password. Same visual
       structure as UserDetail.razor's Reset Password modal (overlay +
       dialog + header/body/footer) so admins get the same UX whether
       they're on the list page or the detail page.

       Admin-only (the button that opens this modal is gated by
       `_isAdmin && !_isViewingSelf`). The handler enforces
       [RequireRoles(Admin)] server-side as defense-in-depth, and Identity's
       password-complexity rules are the final authority on what's accepted.

       State mirrors UserDetail.razor's Reset Password modal:
         - _isResetPasswordModalOpen — controls visibility
         - _resetPasswordTarget    — the UserListItemDto being reset
         - _resetPasswordInput     — the new password being typed
         - _resetPasswordError     — inline validation message
         - _showResetPassword      — show/hide toggle for the password box *@
    @if (_isResetPasswordModalOpen)
    {
        <div class="modal-overlay" @onclick="CloseResetPasswordModal" role="presentation">
            <div class="modal-dialog"
                 role="dialog"
                 aria-modal="true"
                 aria-labelledby="reset-password-modal-title"
                 @onclick:stopPropagation="true"
                 @onkeydown="HandleResetPasswordModalKeydownAsync">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h2 id="reset-password-modal-title" class="modal-title">@Loc["ResetPasswordModalTitle"]</h2>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="modal-close-btn"
                            title="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                            aria-label="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                            disabled="@(_isBusyUserId.HasValue)"
                            @onclick="CloseResetPasswordModal">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="modal-body-text">@Loc["ResetPasswordModalBody"]</p>

                    <label class="modal-label" for="reset-password-input">@Loc["ResetPasswordModalLabel"]</label>
                    <div class="modal-password-row">
                        <RadzenTextBox Value="_resetPasswordInput"
                                       ValueChanged="@OnResetPasswordChanged"
                                       id="reset-password-input"
                                       Type="@(_showResetPassword ? "text" : "password")"
                                       Placeholder="@Loc["ResetPasswordModalPlaceholder"]"
                                       Class="modal-password-field"
                                       Style="width: 100%;"
                                       Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId.HasValue)"
                                       autocomplete="new-password"
                                       autofocus />
                        <RadzenButton Icon="@(_showResetPassword ? "visibility_off" : "visibility")"
                                      title="@(_showResetPassword ? Loc["PasswordHide"] : Loc["PasswordShow"])"
                                      aria-label="@(_showResetPassword ? Loc["PasswordHide"] : Loc["PasswordShow"])"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId.HasValue)"
                                      Click="@ToggleResetPasswordVisibility" />
                    </div>
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                        @Loc["ResetPasswordModalHint"]
                    </RadzenText>
                    <div class="modal-validation" role="status" aria-live="polite">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_resetPasswordError))
                        {
                            <span class="modal-validation-error">@_resetPasswordError</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ModalCancel"]"
                                  Icon="close"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                  Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId.HasValue)"
                                  Click="@CloseResetPasswordModal" />
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ResetPasswordModalSubmit"]"
                                  Icon="vpn_key"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId.HasValue)"
                                  Click="@ConfirmResetPasswordAsync" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<UserListItemDto> _users = new();
    private List<string> _availableGroups = new();

    private RadzenDataGrid<UserListItemDto> grid = default!;

    // Filter state — each nullable; null = "no filter" (AllowClear=true
    // on the RadzenDropDown passes null when the user clears).
    // Status and Gender use string keys that are mapped to the actual
    // property type in the filter handler. Group uses the group name
    // string directly.
    private string? _selectedStatusFilter;
    private string? _selectedGenderFilter;
    private string? _selectedGroupFilter;

    // Status filter options — string keys "Active"/"Inactive" (culture-
    // neutral). The display text comes from GetStatusLabel(string) which
    // maps to localized resx values.
    private readonly List<string> _statusFilterOptions = new()
    {
        "Active", "Inactive"
    };

    // Gender filter options — Key is "Male"/"Female" (culture-neutral),
    // Label is the localized display text.
    private List<GenderFilterOption> _genderFilterOptions = new();

    private sealed class GenderFilterOption
    {
        public string Key { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The Id of the user whose action button is currently in flight.
    /// Null when no action is pending. Used to disable that row's action
    /// buttons while the round-trip is in progress (prevents double-clicks).
    /// Also gates the Reset Password modal's buttons (Cancel/Submit/Close/
    /// show-hide toggle) — when a password reset is in flight, those buttons
    /// are disabled so the user can't accidentally close the modal mid-flight.
    /// </summary>
    private Guid? _isBusyUserId;

    // ── Reset Password modal state ────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Mirrors UserDetail.razor's Reset Password modal state 1:1 (same names,
    // same semantics) so the two pages render identical UX.

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the Reset Password modal is open. Toggled by
    /// HandleResetPasswordAsync (open) and CloseResetPasswordModal /
    /// ConfirmResetPasswordAsync (close).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isResetPasswordModalOpen;

    /// <summary>
    /// The user targeted by the open Reset Password modal. Null when the
    /// modal is closed. Set in HandleResetPasswordAsync + cleared in
    /// CloseResetPasswordModal / ConfirmResetPasswordAsync (on success).
    /// </summary>
    private UserListItemDto? _resetPasswordTarget;

    /// <summary>
    /// The new password currently typed into the modal's RadzenTextBox.
    /// Bound via the explicit ValueChanged callback (OnResetPasswordChanged)
    /// — see that method's remark for why we don't use @bind-Value here.
    /// Cleared when the modal closes.
    /// </summary>
    private string _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline validation message shown below the modal's password box.
    /// Populated by ValidateResetPasswordInput when Submit is clicked.
    /// Empty string when the input is valid (or not yet validated).
    /// </summary>
    private string _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles the password box between masked (default) and plaintext.
    /// Mirrors CreateUser.razor's _showPassword pattern. Purely a UX
    /// affordance — doesn't affect validation or submission.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _showResetPassword;

    /// <summary>
    /// The current user's Id — used to hide self-action buttons
    /// (self-deactivation, self-password-reset) on the user's own row.
    /// </summary>
    private Guid _currentUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Admin role. Computed via
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for everyone in
    /// interactive Blazor Server mode because HttpContext is null over
    /// the SignalR circuit).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Manager role (and NOT also in
    /// the Admin role). Used to gate the activate/deactivate button:
    /// a Manager can only act on users in the Employee OR Customer role —
    /// other managers, admins, and read-onlys are off-limits. Admins (who
    /// may also be in the Manager role) bypass this restriction, so we
    /// explicitly check `!_isAdmin` here.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isManagerOnly;

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Populate the gender-filter dropdown options from localizer.
        _genderFilterOptions = new List<GenderFilterOption>
        {
            new() { Key = "Male",   Label = Loc["GenderMale"] },
            new() { Key = "Female", Label = Loc["GenderFemale"] }
        };

        // Resolve the current user's Id + Admin/Manager roles via the Blazor auth
        // state (NOT ICurrentUserService — see field doc on _isAdmin).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;

            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                var idClaim = user.FindFirst("UserId")?.Value
                              ?? user.FindFirst(System.Security.Claims.ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
                if (Guid.TryParse(idClaim, out var parsedId))
                {
                    _currentUserId = parsedId;
                }

                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
                // Manager-only means "in Manager role AND not also Admin".
                // Admins who happen to also be in the Manager role are
                // treated as Admins (no restriction).
                _isManagerOnly = !_isAdmin && user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _currentUserId stays Guid.Empty (no self-action
            // buttons hidden, which is safe but slightly worse UX) and
            // _isAdmin stays false (Reset Password button hidden — safer
            // fallback if role resolution fails). _isManagerOnly also
            // stays false (no Manager restriction applied — admins always
            // pass through, which is the safer fallback).
        }

        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadUsersAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            // Load all users — filtering and paging are client-side via
            // Radzen's built-in filter row + pager (same approach as the
            // ERP SalesList page). PageSize=500 ensures we get everything
            // in one round-trip.
            var query = new GetUsersPaginatedQuery
            {
                PageNumber = 1,
                PageSize = 500
            };

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<PaginatedResult<UserListItemDto>>(query);

            _users = result.Items.ToList();

            // Derive the available groups from the loaded users for the
            // group filter dropdown. Only non-empty, distinct group names.
            _availableGroups = _users
                .Select(u => u.GroupName)
                .Where(g => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(g))
                .Select(g => g!)
                .Distinct()
                .OrderBy(g => g)
                .ToList();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = ErrorDisplay.Unexpected(UnexpectedErrorCodes.AdminUsers_LoadFailure);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Filter handlers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Each handler sets column.FilterValue and calls grid.Reload() to
    // trigger Radzen's client-side filtering. The bound field is updated
    // by @bind-Value before the Change event fires, so we pass the field
    // (not the args parameter) to the handler.

    private async Task OnStatusFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<UserListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedStatusFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else
        {
            // Map the string key to a boolean for the IsActive column.
            column.FilterValue = value == "Active";
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    private async Task OnGenderFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<UserListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedGenderFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else
        {
            // Map the string key to the Gender enum for the Gender column.
            column.FilterValue = value == "Male"
                ? Domain.Users.Gender.Male
                : Domain.Users.Gender.Female;
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    private async Task OnGroupFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<UserListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedGroupFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else
        {
            column.FilterValue = value;
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    // ── Activate / Deactivate ───────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns true if the current user may activate/deactivate the given
    /// row's user.
    ///
    /// Rules:
    ///   - Admins  → may act on anyone (except themselves, which is checked
    ///               separately in the markup).
    ///   - Managers → may only act on users whose <c>Roles</c> collection
    ///                contains <c>Roles.Employee</c> OR <c>Roles.Customer</c>.
    ///                This excludes other managers, admins, and read-onlys.
    ///   - Employees → cannot activate/deactivate anyone (the feature is
    ///                Admin/Manager only). Returns false for all rows.
    ///
    /// The server-side handlers (ActivateUserCommandHandler /
    /// DeactivateUserCommandHandler) enforce the same rule as
    /// defense-in-depth against tampered requests.
    /// </summary>
    private bool CanActOn(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        // Admins can act on anyone (the markup already hides the button on
        // the admin's own row — we don't re-check that here).
        if (_isAdmin) return true;

        // Managers (non-Admin) can act on Employees OR Customers.
        if (_isManagerOnly)
        {
            return user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Employee)
                || user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Customer);
        }

        // Employees (and anyone else) — cannot activate/deactivate anyone.
        // The markup hides the button entirely for non-Admin/Manager viewers.
        return false;
    }

    private async Task HandleDeactivateAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        // Custom in-app confirmation dialog (DeactivateUserDialog) with a
        // 3-second countdown on the confirm button — same pattern as the
        // sale-cancel flow (CancelConfirmationDialog). Replaces the old
        // window.confirm() call, which gave a sparse native browser popup
        // that didn't match the app's styling and had no friction against
        // reflex confirmations.
        //
        // Rationale for the countdown: deactivation IS reversible (re-run
        // Activate), but it blocks the target user from logging in — which
        // could be a mistake if the admin clicked the wrong row. The
        // 3-second pause is enough to catch a reflex click.
        //
        // The handler also rejects self-deactivation as defense-in-depth,
        // but we hide the button on the user's own row anyway (see markup).
        object? confirmed;
        try
        {
            confirmed = await DialogService.OpenAsync<DeactivateUserDialog>(
                Loc["DeactivateDialogTitle"],
                new Dictionary<string, object?>
                {
                    { "UserDisplayName", user.FullName }
                },
                new Radzen.DialogOptions
                {
                    Width = "420px",
                    Resizable = false,
                    Draggable = true,
                    CloseDialogOnOverlayClick = false,  // force the user to click a button — no accidental close
                    ShowClose = true,                   // keep the X button so the user has an obvious escape
                });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // DialogService.OpenAsync shouldn't throw under normal use, but
            // if it does (e.g. JS-interop failure), surface it instead of
            // silently swallowing.
            System.Diagnostics.Debug.WriteLine($"HandleDeactivateAsync: dialog open failed: {ex}");
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.AdminUsers_DialogOpen, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // `confirmed` is `object?` (boxed bool from DialogService.Close(true|false),
        // or null if the user dismissed via X / Esc / overlay). Anything that
        // isn't exactly `true` is treated as "user aborted".
        if (confirmed is not true) return;

        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeactivateUserCommand(user.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["DeactivateSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["DeactivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadUsersAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // The handler rejects self-deactivation with a friendly
                // message; surface it verbatim.
                await Toast.Error(
                    ErrorDisplay.Localize(result.Error) ?? Loc["ActionError"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.AdminUsers_DeactivateFailure, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleActivateAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        // No confirmation for activation — it's a non-destructive restore.
        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ActivateUserCommand(user.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActivateSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["ActivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadUsersAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    ErrorDisplay.Localize(result.Error) ?? Loc["ActionError"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.AdminUsers_ActivateFailure, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Reset password (Admin only) ─────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The flow uses an INLINE MODAL (mirrors UserDetail.razor's Reset Password
    // modal — same HTML/CSS/keys) instead of the previous JS prompt(). JS
    // prompt() was ugly, unstyled, un-themeable, and didn't render localized
    // text correctly in some browsers. The modal gives us:
    //   1. A styled dialog that matches the rest of the app's UX.
    //   2. A password input with show/hide toggle.
    //   3. Inline validation messaging (no Toast.Warning on bad input).
    //   4. Cancel + Submit buttons (no accidental dismiss via Esc/click-out).
    //
    // State variables (defined alongside _isBusyUserId above):
    //   _isResetPasswordModalOpen — controls modal visibility
    //   _resetPasswordTarget      — the UserListItemDto being reset (null when modal closed)
    //   _resetPasswordInput       — the new password being typed
    //   _resetPasswordError       — inline validation message (empty when valid)
    //   _showResetPassword        — show/hide toggle for the password box
    //
    // The handler defers password-complexity validation to ASP.NET Identity's
    // configured rules. Client-side, we just check non-empty + ≥ 8 chars to
    // catch obvious typos before the round-trip (same as UserDetail.razor).

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the Reset Password modal for the given user. Stores the target
    /// user so ConfirmResetPasswordAsync knows which account to reset. Clears
    /// any previous input + error so the modal starts fresh each time.
    /// Called from the "Reset password" button in the row's Actions column.
    /// </summary>
    private void HandleResetPasswordAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        _resetPasswordTarget = user;
        _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;
        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        _showResetPassword = false;
        _isResetPasswordModalOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Closes the Reset Password modal without saving. Called by the Cancel
    /// button, the X close button, and the Escape key handler. Clears all
    /// modal state so the next open starts fresh.
    /// </summary>
    private void CloseResetPasswordModal()
    {
        // Don't allow closing while a request is in flight — the server
        // might be mid-reset and we don't want to lose track of the result.
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        _isResetPasswordModalOpen = false;
        _resetPasswordTarget = null;
        _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;
        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        _showResetPassword = false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Keydown handler for the Reset Password modal. Closes the modal on
    /// Escape (same UX as UserDetail.razor's modal). Enter is NOT bound
    /// here because the password input's own Enter handling submits the
    /// form implicitly via the Submit button.
    /// </summary>
    private Task HandleResetPasswordModalKeydownAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e.Key == "Escape")
        {
            CloseResetPasswordModal();
        }
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Bound to the password box's ValueChanged callback so we can toggle
    /// the input type between Text and Password without losing the value
    /// (RadzenTextBox @bind-Value doesn't round-trip through the Type change
    /// cleanly — this explicit ValueChanged pattern is more reliable).
    /// Same pattern as CreateUser.razor's OnPasswordChanged.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnResetPasswordChanged(string value)
    {
        _resetPasswordInput = value ?? string.Empty;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles the password visibility between masked and plaintext.
    /// Mirrors CreateUser.razor's TogglePasswordVisibility.
    /// </summary>
    private Task ToggleResetPasswordVisibility()
    {
        _showResetPassword = !_showResetPassword;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Validates _resetPasswordInput. Returns true if valid (and populates
    /// _resetPasswordError for inline display if invalid). Minimal client-
    /// side check — Identity's complexity rules are the real authority.
    /// </summary>
    private bool ValidateResetPasswordInput()
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_resetPasswordInput))
        {
            _resetPasswordError = Loc["ResetPasswordRequiredError"];
            return false;
        }

        if (_resetPasswordInput.Length < 8)
        {
            _resetPasswordError = Loc["ResetPasswordLengthError"];
            return false;
        }

        _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
        return true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Submit handler for the Reset Password modal. Validates the input; if
    /// valid, dispatches ResetUserPasswordCommand via Wolverine. On success,
    /// shows a toast + closes the modal. On failure, surfaces Identity's
    /// error description verbatim (they're user-friendly).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ConfirmResetPasswordAsync()
    {
        if (_resetPasswordTarget is null) return;

        if (!ValidateResetPasswordInput()) return;

        var target = _resetPasswordTarget;
        var newPassword = _resetPasswordInput;

        _isBusyUserId = target.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ResetUserPasswordCommand(target.Id, newPassword));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ResetSuccess"], target.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["ResetSuccessTitle"]);

                // Close the modal + clear state.
                _isResetPasswordModalOpen = false;
                _resetPasswordTarget = null;
                _resetPasswordInput = string.Empty;
                _resetPasswordError = string.Empty;
                _showResetPassword = false;
            }
            else
            {
                // Identity's error descriptions are user-friendly (e.g.
                // "Passwords must have at least one non-alphanumeric character.")
                // — surface verbatim in the inline validation slot so the
                // user can fix + retry without losing their typed value.
                _resetPasswordError = result.Error ?? Loc["ResetError"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _resetPasswordError = Loc["ResetError"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Row render hook ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void OnRowRender(RowRenderEventArgs<UserListItemDto> args)
    {
        // Subtle visual cue for inactive rows: slight opacity. The status
        // badge already conveys the state, but the row-level cue helps
        // scan-by-gesture users notice deactivated accounts at a glance.
        if (args.Data is { } u && !u.IsActive)
        {
            args.Attributes.Add("style", "opacity: 0.65;");
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string GetGenderLabel(Domain.Users.Gender gender)
        => gender switch
        {
            Domain.Users.Gender.Male => Loc["GenderMale"],
            Domain.Users.Gender.Female => Loc["GenderFemale"],
            _ => gender.ToString()
        };

    // String overload — used by the gender filter dropdown's ValueTemplate
    // and Template. Maps "Male"/"Female" keys to localized display text.
    private string GetGenderLabel(string? key)
        => key switch
        {
            "Male" => Loc["GenderMale"],
            "Female" => Loc["GenderFemale"],
            _ => Loc["GenderAll"]
        };

    // Returns inline CSS for the gender badge background color.
    // Male=blue (#2196f3), Female=pink (#e91e63). Used by both the cell
    // Template and the filter dropdown's ValueTemplate/Template so they
    // always render the same color.
    private string GetGenderBadgeStyle(Domain.Users.Gender gender)
        => gender switch
        {
            Domain.Users.Gender.Male => "background: #2196f3; color: white;",
            Domain.Users.Gender.Female => "background: #e91e63; color: white;",
            _ => ""
        };

    // String overload — maps "Male"/"Female" keys to the same colors.
    private string GetGenderBadgeStyle(string? key)
        => key switch
        {
            "Male" => "background: #2196f3; color: white;",
            "Female" => "background: #e91e63; color: white;",
            _ => ""
        };

    // ── Status helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Used by both the cell Template (bool overload — user.IsActive) and
    // the filter dropdown's ValueTemplate/Template (string overload —
    // "Active"/"Inactive" keys).

    private string GetStatusLabel(bool isActive)
        => isActive ? Loc["StatusActiveBadge"] : Loc["StatusInactiveBadge"];

    private string GetStatusLabel(string? status)
        => status switch
        {
            "Active" => Loc["StatusActive"],
            "Inactive" => Loc["StatusInactive"],
            _ => Loc["StatusAll"]
        };

    private BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(bool isActive)
        => isActive ? BadgeStyle.Success : BadgeStyle.Danger;

    private BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(string? status)
        => status switch
        {
            "Active" => BadgeStyle.Success,
            "Inactive" => BadgeStyle.Danger,
            _ => BadgeStyle.Base
        };
}